Abstract
Stiff Person Syndrome (SPS), a progressive Central Nervous System disorder is 
accompanied by progressive muscle rigidity, hyperreflexia, and spasms mainly in 
truncal and proximal leg muscles mainly associated with autoimmune disorders. 
Here, we report a rare case of SPS in a middle- aged Nepalese man with uncon-
trolled diabetes mellitus and ketonuria.
